      <Desc>SANFORD LABORATORIES FOR INNOVATIVE MEDICINES (SANFORD LABS) IS AN INDEPENDENT, NOT-FOR-PROFIT COLLABORATIVE HUB WITH A MISSION TO ACCELERATE THE DEVELOPMENT OF NOVEL MOLECULAR MEDICINES FROM SCIENTIFIC DISCOVERY TO THE CLINIC. OUR CURRENT RESEARCH IS FOCUSED ON RNA THERAPEUTICS, A RAPIDLY EXPANDING CLASS OF DRUGS WITH THE POTENTIAL TO PROGRESS QUICKLY FROM CONCEPT TO PATIENT AND CHANGE THE STANDARD OF CARE FOR MANY LIFE-THREATENING DISEASES. (CONTINUED ON SCHEDULE O).OUR UNIQUE OPERATING MODEL FILLS A CRITICAL GAP FOR TRANSLATIONAL RESEARCH THAT DOES NOT FIT TRADITIONAL ACADEMIC LABS AND YET IS TOO EARLY FOR VENTURE OR INDUSTRY INVESTMENT. OUR RESEARCH TEAMS, LED BY TEAMS OF ENTREPRENEURIAL SCIENTISTS, ARE ORGANIZED AROUND THERAPEUTIC APPROACHES AND PLATFORM TECHNOLOGIES WITH BROAD APPLICABILITY TO A RANGE OF DISEASES, THUS ENABLING THE EFFICIENT PROTOTYPING OF MULTIPLE NEW MEDICINES IN PARALLEL. IN ADDITION TO OUR INTERNAL RESEARCH, WE ARE ACTIVELY FORGING COLLABORATIONS ACROSS THE DYNAMIC LIFE SCIENCE ECOSYSTEM AND AIM TO ENHANCE SAN DIEGO'S LEADERSHIP AS A WORLD-CLASS CLUSTER IN RNA BIOLOGY AND MEDICINES.</Desc>
