      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 12C</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>SANFORD LABS REGULARLY AND CONSISTENTLY MONITORS AND ENFORCES THESE POLICIES IN ACCORDANCE WITH WRITTEN PROCEDURES. DUTY TO DISCLOSE. IN CONNECTION WITH ANY ACTUAL OR POSSIBLE CONFLICT OF INTEREST, AN INTERESTED PERSON MUST DISCLOSE THE EXISTENCE OF THE FINANCIAL INTEREST AND BE GIVEN THE OPPORTUNITY TO DISCLOSE ALL MATERIAL FACTS TO THE DIRECTORS AND/OR THE MEMBERS OF APPROPRIATE COMMITTEES WITH BOARD DELEGATED POWERS, IF ANY, CONSIDERING THE PROPOSED TRANSACTION OR ARRANGEMENT. ANY BOARD MEMBER WITH A CONFLICT IS NOT ALLOWED TO VOTE ON THE TRANSACTION.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>FORM 990, PART VI, SECTION B, LINE 15</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>SANFORD LABS ENGAGED A HUMAN RESOURCE CONSULTANT TO DETERMINE A SALARY RANGE FOR OFFICERS BASED ON COMPARABLE ORGANIZATIONS AND INDUSTRY. ALL INDEPENDENT BOARD MEMBERS REVIEW AND APPROVE THE RANGES, AND ANY SALARY INCREASES. EACH OFFICER HAS AN EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT APPROVED BY THE INDEPENDENT BOARD DIRECTORS. THIS PROCESS LAST OCCURRED IN NOVEMBER 2024.</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
